      "raw": "[quote=\"Greywind\"]\n2) Yes.\n[/quote]\n\nTo clarify, I&#39;m fairly certain that the revealed card is not on the top of the deck while you&#39;re Enlightening yourself.&nbsp; Effects such as Infrared Eyepiece say to &quot;put one on the top of the deck (and the other on the bottom)&quot;, which would be redundant if they stayed on the top of the deck after being revealed.&nbsp; So I think they go to a sort of &quot;in-between zone&quot;, not in play or in a deck or trash, while the effects of a card are resolving.&nbsp; You should then always have instructions telling you what to do with the card...if no such instructions existed, I don&#39;t know what would happen.&nbsp; If anyone can think of a card that doesn&#39;t provide any, it might serve as a counterexample to what I&#39;m proposing.\n",
