      "id": 81307,
      "name": "Kingofsouls",
      "username": "Kingofsouls",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/58f4c7/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-10T05:45:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It spesifically says \"reveal the top card of your deck\".. To me, that translates to&nbsp; \"You get to see what the top card is and it still techically is in the deck.\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>what trips me up is teh dicard clause. Does the revealed card get discarded no matter if its on the deck, in your hand, in the in-between area you mentined, or anythign else? That's the big question.</p>",
