      "raw": "<p>It spesifically says &quot;reveal the top card of your deck&quot;.. To me, that translates to&nbsp; &quot;You get to see what the top card is and it still techically is in the deck.&quot;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>what trips me up is teh dicard clause. Does the revealed card get discarded no matter if its on the deck, in your hand, in the in-between area you mentined, or anythign else? That&#39;s the big question.</p>",
