    {
      "id": 81308,
      "name": "Envisioner",
      "username": "Envisioner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-11-10T05:50:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Kingofsouls\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Kingofsouls:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It spesifically says \"reveal the top card of your deck\"… To me, that translates to&nbsp; \"You get to see what the top card is and it still techically is in the deck.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It <em>was</em> the top card of your deck before being revealed; whether it still is afterward remains a bit unclear, but as I've said, it seems most consistent with other cards to assume that \"revealed\" is a sort of game-zone in itself, apart from decks and play areas.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>what trips me up is teh dicard clause. Does the revealed card get discarded no matter if its on the deck, in your hand, in the in-between area you mentined, or anythign else? That's the big question.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It's true that the word \"discard\" usually signifies only \"put to trash from hand\", but I'm pretty sure all of Misty's spells which have this clause say \"Put the revealed card into your trash\".&nbsp; I'm not 100% certain the card can't be the first one you draw when Enlightening yourself, but I've never played it that way and I would be surprised if anyone else does.&nbsp; Certainly the ability to draw up to four cards while damaging something (yourself if you don't have The Amulet or cards to power it) is critically useful to her deck's mechanism; if she couldn't get that first card, it'd be a significant hindrance to her.&nbsp; (Then again, I have found her to be extremely powerful when playing \"my way\", so perhaps I was doing her an unjustified favor?&nbsp; But I still doubt it.)</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:03:43.177Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
