      "raw": "[quote=\"Kingofsouls\"]\n\nIt spesifically says &quot;reveal the top card of your deck&quot;.. To me, that translates to&nbsp; &quot;You get to see what the top card is and it still techically is in the deck.&quot;\n[/quote]\n\nIt <em>was</em> the top card of your deck before being revealed; whether it still is afterward remains a bit unclear, but as I&#39;ve said, it seems most consistent with other cards to assume that &quot;revealed&quot; is a sort of game-zone in itself, apart from decks and play areas.\n\n> what trips me up is teh dicard clause. Does the revealed card get discarded no matter if its on the deck, in your hand, in the in-between area you mentined, or anythign else? That&#39;s the big question.\n\nIt&#39;s true that the word &quot;discard&quot; usually signifies only &quot;put to trash from hand&quot;, but I&#39;m pretty sure all of Misty&#39;s spells which have this clause say &quot;Put the revealed card into your trash&quot;.&nbsp; I&#39;m not 100% certain the card can&#39;t be the first one you draw when Enlightening yourself, but I&#39;ve never played it that way and I would be surprised if anyone else does.&nbsp; Certainly the ability to draw up to four cards while damaging something (yourself if you don&#39;t have The Amulet or cards to power it) is critically useful to her deck&#39;s mechanism; if she couldn&#39;t get that first card, it&#39;d be a significant hindrance to her.&nbsp; (Then again, I have found her to be extremely powerful when playing &quot;my way&quot;, so perhaps I was doing her an unjustified favor?&nbsp; But I still doubt it.)\n",
