      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Revealed cards are not considered part of the deck. When you reveal cards, they get revealed in the play area. Enlighten would not have you draw the card you just revealed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's certainly the way I've always played it, but what's your source for actually determining that to be true ruleswise?</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:03:43.425Z",
